1
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:54,430
How did you find me?

2
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,764
The bag.

3
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,349
Your bag.

4
00:00:57,349 --> 00:01:00,185
- What?
- It kept fluttering by.

5
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,728
Like a butterfly.

6
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:03,454
So I followed it.

7
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:12,092
- Think you can pull it off?
- Me?

8
00:01:12,092 --> 00:01:13,564
Wait.

9
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:17,938
Ha Yeon.

10
00:01:45,284 --> 00:01:46,434
Here.

11
00:01:55,199 --> 00:01:58,719
[9. The Feeling of Liking Someone]

12
00:01:59,328 --> 00:02:00,996
Then he suddenly takes my hand.

13
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:03,238
Really?

14
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:07,702
Hey.

15
00:02:07,702 --> 00:02:08,763
What?

16
00:02:08,763 --> 00:02:10,193
Kim Ha Yeon.

17
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:15,103
Hello? Maid material?

18
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:20,804
Hey.

19
00:02:20,804 --> 00:02:22,809
I heard you were going to die?

20
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,540
But why are you still alive?

21
00:02:26,313 --> 00:02:28,022
It just turned out that way.

22
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:32,054
Seriously. Then don't vow things like that
so lightly.

23
00:02:32,054 --> 00:02:34,363
I got my hopes up for nothing.

24
00:02:34,363 --> 00:02:36,934
Hey. I'll see you after summer break.

25
00:02:36,934 --> 00:02:39,044
I won't let you off the hook.

26
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:41,286
No.

27
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:43,285
Why wait until after?

28
00:02:43,285 --> 00:02:44,766
Let's do it now.

29
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:49,753
- What?
- And if you don't let me off, then what?

30
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:51,665
Just try it right now.

31
00:02:52,297 --> 00:02:54,179
I'm really excited for it too.

32
00:02:54,179 --> 00:02:55,884
Hey!

33
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:58,119
Don't yell.

34
00:02:58,119 --> 00:03:00,713
I can hear you fine without that.

35
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:04,302
- You...
- What are you doing?

36
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:08,896
It's nothing.

37
00:03:08,896 --> 00:03:10,012
Let's go.

38
00:03:10,012 --> 00:03:11,032
Okay.

39
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,871
Seriously. What is that?

40
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:27,749
- Come on. You hungry?
- I don't know.

41
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,450
Does she have a brother?

42
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,404
She does. Her brother's in college.

43
00:03:33,797 --> 00:03:38,135
So she's here stuffing burgers
with her brother?

44
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:39,940
I don't know either.

45
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:45,377
But Yun Ah, do you really think
that guy is Ha Yeon's brother?

46
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:51,605
- Is it good?
- Yes.

47
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,617
I should eat some too.

48
00:04:00,282 --> 00:04:02,006
[Episode 9]

49
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:05,328
I saw you.

50
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,150
- Me?
- You're a good swimmer.

51
00:04:07,150 --> 00:04:08,415
You're a good swimmer.

52
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:10,190
- Have you seen this?
- Yes.

53
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:11,570
Sit here, you guys.

54
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:12,702
- What?
- Why stand?

55
00:04:12,702 --> 00:04:14,077
- No, sit.
- Your seat?

56
00:04:14,077 --> 00:04:15,839
- No, no. It's fine.
- Sit down?

57
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,054
Yes, you can sit.

58
00:04:17,054 --> 00:04:18,467
- We can sit?
- Sit.

59
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:19,509
- Thanks.
- Thank you.

60
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:20,761
We're all swimmers.

61
00:04:20,761 --> 00:04:22,689
Looks like you two broke up today.

62
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:24,880
Look.

63
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:28,435
I get confused every time,
so I have even asked Cho Yu Gyeom.

64
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:31,990
But every time, he wouldn't
give me a straight answer.

65
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:36,250
But today even I can tell for sure.

66
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:38,490
That you two broke up today.

67
00:04:38,490 --> 00:04:40,270
Get lost.

68
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:44,784
You know, I'm really not the type
to feel inferior at all.

69
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:47,204
But with Cho Yu Gyeom, I'm starting to.

70
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:48,463
Why?

71
00:04:48,463 --> 00:04:51,824
Because he's always good at what I like.

72
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:53,930
Jeong Uk.

73
00:04:53,930 --> 00:04:56,230
That's just fate.

74
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:57,381
What?

75
00:04:57,381 --> 00:04:58,757
It's fate.

76
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:01,161
A fate you were born with.

77
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:06,723
So you're always coming in second,
while Cho Yu Gyeom comes in first.

78
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:09,100
That was decided from the day you were born.

79
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,970
And that will never flip halfway through.

80
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:13,376
Got it?

81
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:19,170
But even I never thought
someone as pretty as you...

82
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:22,852
would end up an outcast
getting hit with water bombs.

83
00:05:22,852 --> 00:05:24,059
Hey.

84
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:28,010
Our lives are long.

85
00:05:28,010 --> 00:05:29,614
You never know.

86
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:31,789
You said so yourself.

87
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:37,030
No. That aside, Cho Yu Gyeom
will always outshine you.

88
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:40,070
I might not shine as much as he does.

89
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:43,186
But I wouldn't send my girlfriend
home alone like this.

90
00:05:44,910 --> 00:05:46,262
And...

91
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:51,289
I wouldn't stand next to my girlfriend
with a crappy look like that.

92
00:05:58,410 --> 00:06:00,142
Yu Gyeom.

93
00:06:00,142 --> 00:06:01,304
Yes?

94
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:07,266
Shall we listen to that music?

95
00:06:07,266 --> 00:06:09,640
The one we heard here that time.

96
00:06:10,961 --> 00:06:12,246
Let's do that.

97
00:06:23,634 --> 00:06:24,965
Yu Gyeom.

98
00:06:24,965 --> 00:06:29,079
They say there are three things
a person can never hide.

99
00:06:34,006 --> 00:06:40,006
A cough, poverty,
and the feeling of liking someone.

100
00:07:26,986 --> 00:07:31,972
As for me, you caught me liking you.

101
00:07:43,172 --> 00:07:44,516
Seriously!

102
00:07:45,126 --> 00:07:47,092
Come on!

103
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:49,626
Kim Jung Yeon!

104
00:07:49,626 --> 00:07:51,930
What did Kim Ha Yeon tell you?

105
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:53,426
Staying at a friend's.

106
00:07:53,426 --> 00:07:55,726
Seriously!

107
00:07:55,726 --> 00:07:59,453
Has she completely lost her mind?

108
00:07:59,453 --> 00:08:02,886
Why tell you that? She should tell me!

109
00:08:02,886 --> 00:08:05,145
That's because you would say no.

110
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:09,448
Seriously. She doesn't have any friends!

111
00:08:09,448 --> 00:08:11,328
She's an outcast.

112
00:08:13,169 --> 00:08:15,221
You knew?

113
00:08:15,221 --> 00:08:17,438
Of course I knew!

114
00:08:17,438 --> 00:08:19,249
Then why did you just let it slide?

115
00:08:19,249 --> 00:08:24,939
Hey! Because she didn't say anything!
I thought she was fine!

116
00:08:27,023 --> 00:08:28,810
Not a word.

117
00:08:30,938 --> 00:08:34,643
Just because she's silent
doesn't mean she's okay.

118
00:08:35,659 --> 00:08:37,059
What did you say?

119
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:39,198
I'm saying, she doesn't say...

120
00:08:42,910 --> 00:08:47,342
[You don't have to send us more money.
We're fine]

121
00:08:48,413 --> 00:08:51,416
How is staying silent okay?

122
00:08:51,416 --> 00:08:54,766
She could be festering and rotting inside.

123
00:08:54,766 --> 00:08:59,696
If you knew Kim Ha Yeon was an outcast,
you should have protected her.

124
00:08:59,696 --> 00:09:02,719
How could you just stand by and watch?

125
00:09:03,544 --> 00:09:07,699
Now, you're blaming me too?

126
00:09:09,626 --> 00:09:11,430
Mom...

127
00:09:12,774 --> 00:09:17,222
Be glad she didn't die, count yourself lucky.

128
00:09:24,946 --> 00:09:26,065
Hey!

129
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:27,827
Kim Jung Yeon!

130
00:09:28,566 --> 00:09:30,241
Seriously.

131
00:09:54,887 --> 00:09:57,023
Where were you yesterday?

132
00:09:58,139 --> 00:10:00,830
- The lodge...
- You entered the competition.

133
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:02,862
And skipped the ancestral rite.

134
00:10:05,312 --> 00:10:07,294
Nothing to say?

135
00:10:08,341 --> 00:10:09,689
Yes.

136
00:10:09,689 --> 00:10:12,636
You can't even say you're sorry?

137
00:10:14,146 --> 00:10:15,272
Yes.

138
00:10:17,706 --> 00:10:19,946
I'm not sorry, Grandfather.

139
00:10:19,946 --> 00:10:21,342
I see.

140
00:10:21,342 --> 00:10:25,365
Back then, your father
said the same thing to me.

141
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:28,986
No.

142
00:10:28,986 --> 00:10:30,547
I'm not sorry,

143
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:31,886
Father.

144
00:10:34,706 --> 00:10:38,013
And so he went to the Olympics.

145
00:10:38,013 --> 00:10:42,046
Like father, like son. You're exactly the same.

146
00:10:42,046 --> 00:10:43,632
Grandfather.

147
00:10:43,632 --> 00:10:45,095
It's not even the Olympics. I just...

148
00:10:45,095 --> 00:10:47,730
Right. That's how it starts.

149
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,291
"Just this once."

150
00:10:50,291 --> 00:10:53,427
"Yes, just this one time."

151
00:10:53,427 --> 00:10:58,426
In the end, you go all the way
and give up right before the goal.

152
00:10:58,426 --> 00:11:01,703
All the way there,
your father didn't know a thing.

153
00:11:01,703 --> 00:11:02,728
Right?

154
00:11:02,728 --> 00:11:08,539
He kept saying "just once, just once,"
and lost so many precious things.

155
00:11:08,539 --> 00:11:11,296
Your father never realized it.

156
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:15,268
Back then, he lost what
he should have cherished.

157
00:11:15,268 --> 00:11:18,246
His lover. His friends. Even his family.

158
00:11:18,246 --> 00:11:22,022
If you do the same as your father,
you'll surely lose something too.

159
00:11:22,022 --> 00:11:24,589
The more you do, the more
precious things you'll lose.

160
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,046
All right.

161
00:11:27,046 --> 00:11:30,575
- Yu Gyeom, what will you lose?
- You, Grandfather.

162
00:11:31,821 --> 00:11:33,177
What?

163
00:11:33,177 --> 00:11:34,566
So I'll lose you, Grandfather.

164
00:11:34,566 --> 00:11:35,946
Say that again.

165
00:11:35,946 --> 00:11:38,944
I said I'll lose you. If I lose just you...

166
00:11:41,287 --> 00:11:43,532
I can have everything, can't I?

167
00:11:56,698 --> 00:11:59,024
Please help me, Jung Yeon.

168
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:06,177
But Noh Si Ha, you shouldn't do this to me.

169
00:12:16,996 --> 00:12:19,049
Someone fell outside.

170
00:12:19,049 --> 00:12:20,324
Someone fell!

171
00:12:20,324 --> 00:12:22,799
- Someone fell?
- Really?

172
00:12:23,744 --> 00:12:26,233
- It's true.
- I'm scared.

173
00:12:27,172 --> 00:12:28,566
Really?

174
00:12:36,035 --> 00:12:38,696
The person who fell is Noh Si Ha!

175
00:12:38,696 --> 00:12:40,696
- Noh Si Ha from our department?
- What?

176
00:12:40,696 --> 00:12:41,756
I said Noh Si Ha.

177
00:12:41,756 --> 00:12:43,436
Is it really Noh Si Ha?

178
00:12:43,436 --> 00:12:45,250
I think so.

179
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:47,236
What do we do? Call it in.

180
00:12:47,236 --> 00:12:49,480
I can't. Do it for me.

181
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,713
Sure.

182
00:12:59,416 --> 00:13:01,713
What do we do?

183
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,800
What do we do?

184
00:13:20,416 --> 00:13:23,462
Jung Yeon, what are you up to today?

185
00:13:37,996 --> 00:13:39,270
Hey.

186
00:13:40,429 --> 00:13:42,384
Hand over your phone.

187
00:13:44,601 --> 00:13:46,186
Give it here.

188
00:13:46,186 --> 00:13:51,032
Right now Mom doesn't even
have the energy to yell.

189
00:14:04,604 --> 00:14:10,562
Depending on how you act, I'll give this back.

190
00:14:13,508 --> 00:14:14,937
Listen, Ha Yeon.

191
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:15,981
Yes.

192
00:14:15,981 --> 00:14:22,028
You asked me whether I was
also a total mess at your age.

193
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:25,683
I seemed fine on the outside but not inside.

194
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:31,455
So I thought long and hard about it.

195
00:14:31,455 --> 00:14:32,954
But...

196
00:14:33,771 --> 00:14:35,176
No.

197
00:14:35,176 --> 00:14:36,255
Me?

198
00:14:36,255 --> 00:14:37,776
I was fine.

199
00:14:37,776 --> 00:14:39,219
I was perfectly fine.

200
00:14:39,219 --> 00:14:40,429
Outside, too!

201
00:14:40,429 --> 00:14:42,806
I never acted out like you!

202
00:14:42,806 --> 00:14:44,012
Inside, too!

203
00:14:44,012 --> 00:14:45,416
I was okay.

204
00:14:45,416 --> 00:14:47,471
Perfectly okay.

205
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,456
What's "ah" supposed to mean?

206
00:14:51,456 --> 00:14:56,176
What I'm saying is you're the only
one acting strange right now. Only you.

207
00:14:56,176 --> 00:15:00,073
Your brother, your dad, and I are all fine.

208
00:15:00,696 --> 00:15:02,236
No.

209
00:15:02,236 --> 00:15:03,616
Mom.

210
00:15:03,616 --> 00:15:05,176
Jung Yeon is strange.

211
00:15:05,176 --> 00:15:06,322
What?

212
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,632
Do you really think Jung Yeon looks fine?

213
00:15:08,632 --> 00:15:11,364
What's strange about Jung Yeon?

214
00:15:11,364 --> 00:15:14,101
Jung Yeon is perfectly normal.

215
00:15:15,066 --> 00:15:16,651
He doesn't smile.

216
00:15:18,102 --> 00:15:19,376
What?

217
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:22,880
He never smiles around us at all.

218
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,336
And Dad...

219
00:15:24,336 --> 00:15:25,596
He doesn't do a thing.

220
00:15:25,596 --> 00:15:27,680
What dad is like that these days, Mom?

221
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:30,081
Dad's a little strange too.

222
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:33,656
No, he's not.

223
00:15:33,656 --> 00:15:35,970
To me, you're the only strange one.

224
00:15:36,849 --> 00:15:40,325
Then maybe I'm just a little different.

225
00:15:40,325 --> 00:15:42,233
Are you playing word games with me?

226
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:44,362
Please.

227
00:15:44,362 --> 00:15:46,946
Just accept that people are different.

228
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,750
You're a teacher, Mom.

229
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:50,798
Isn't that basic for an educator?

230
00:15:54,661 --> 00:15:57,869
Hey! Seriously, that girl.

231
00:15:57,869 --> 00:16:01,043
Hey! My daughter stayed out
overnight without permission!

232
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:04,172
Accept what differences? Seriously.

233
00:16:04,172 --> 00:16:05,381
I'm leaving now.

234
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:09,010
I could just...

235
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:11,387
Hey. Kim Jung Yeon.

236
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:13,805
Do you ever smile?

237
00:16:16,727 --> 00:16:18,587
He's gone already?

238
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,105
Good grief!

239
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,073
Cho Yu Gyeom.

240
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:33,236
When's your next race?

241
00:16:33,236 --> 00:16:34,796
Day after tomorrow, morning.

242
00:16:34,796 --> 00:16:35,846
Why?

243
00:16:40,285 --> 00:16:42,300
- Cho Yu Gyeom.
- What?

244
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,577
When do you practice?

245
00:16:43,577 --> 00:16:46,538
I'm not allowed to compete. What practice?

246
00:17:03,071 --> 00:17:06,808
Jung Yeon, you seem tired.

247
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:11,632
No.

248
00:17:11,632 --> 00:17:13,868
Can I try one thing with you?

249
00:17:16,212 --> 00:17:17,994
What are you going to do?

250
00:17:38,956 --> 00:17:42,034
You seem lonely sometimes.

251
00:17:50,257 --> 00:17:52,211
You looked lonely.

252
00:17:57,976 --> 00:18:02,747
I thought that if I did this,
you might feel a little warmer.

253
00:18:10,556 --> 00:18:12,206
I...

254
00:18:14,476 --> 00:18:16,477
I hated her.

255
00:18:21,872 --> 00:18:23,851
I hated her.

256
00:18:27,441 --> 00:18:28,737
I...

257
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,474
There was nothing I could do for her.

258
00:18:35,532 --> 00:18:37,971
And she kept getting on my nerves.

259
00:18:41,177 --> 00:18:43,846
Everything about it got on my nerves.

260
00:18:58,931 --> 00:19:00,313
But...

261
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:07,006
But it's not like she had to die.

262
00:19:08,124 --> 00:19:10,256
Hey, did you hear?

263
00:19:10,256 --> 00:19:14,644
The last person Noh Si Ha
sent a text to was Kim Jung Yeon.

264
00:19:14,644 --> 00:19:15,744
That's creepy.

265
00:19:15,744 --> 00:19:17,969
But I think it was Kim Jung Yeon.

266
00:19:29,904 --> 00:19:32,184
Are you okay?

267
00:19:32,184 --> 00:19:33,244
What?

268
00:19:33,244 --> 00:19:35,524
I mean, that thing with Si Ha.

269
00:19:35,524 --> 00:19:38,404
You don't think she died because of you,
do you?

270
00:19:38,404 --> 00:19:39,650
Right.

271
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:40,984
It's not true.

272
00:19:40,984 --> 00:19:43,890
Yes. I never thought that at all.

273
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:50,040
But since you put it that way...

274
00:19:51,534 --> 00:19:54,111
I wonder if I'm the only
one who didn't think so.

275
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,630
No... I...

276
00:19:57,630 --> 00:19:59,448
I didn't mean it that way.

277
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,818
It's just...

278
00:20:05,205 --> 00:20:07,491
J-Jung Yeon.

279
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:20,084
The thought that...

280
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,015
She died because of me.

281
00:20:27,978 --> 00:20:30,072
It is driving me crazy.

282
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:37,101
So that's why you wanted to talk
to that friend's parents?

283
00:20:40,968 --> 00:20:42,523
Tell me.

284
00:20:44,244 --> 00:20:45,693
Si Ha.

285
00:20:50,682 --> 00:20:53,006
Did she die because of me?

286
00:20:58,099 --> 00:21:00,552
It's not your fault.

287
00:21:00,552 --> 00:21:02,310
It really isn't.

288
00:21:06,475 --> 00:21:10,729
Jung Yeon, shall we go see them together?

289
00:21:10,729 --> 00:21:15,445
If you want to, I'll go with you.

290
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:40,884
Cho Yu Gyeom.

291
00:21:40,884 --> 00:21:42,906
- Come out!
- What?

292
00:21:44,164 --> 00:21:45,673
I said come out.

293
00:21:45,673 --> 00:21:47,035
Why?

294
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:49,192
Aren't you going to practice?

295
00:22:07,132 --> 00:22:11,219
Hey, I opened the pool, so use it until 3 a.m.

296
00:22:11,219 --> 00:22:13,581
And be sure to take first place.

297
00:22:13,581 --> 00:22:17,264
Take first, go to Nationals,
and the Olympics too.

298
00:22:17,264 --> 00:22:19,384
Don't live like me.

299
00:22:20,631 --> 00:22:21,684
Then, Father.

300
00:22:21,684 --> 00:22:23,374
What is it, kid?

301
00:22:24,144 --> 00:22:28,472
If I'm not going to live like you,
I need my phone too.

302
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,473
What? Phone?

303
00:22:30,473 --> 00:22:32,348
Yes, my phone.

304
00:22:32,348 --> 00:22:33,620
My cell phone.

305
00:22:35,744 --> 00:22:38,058
You brat. I'm not giving it back.

306
00:22:38,734 --> 00:22:40,405
I really need it.

307
00:23:01,518 --> 00:23:03,864
This is really nice.

308
00:23:03,864 --> 00:23:05,392
What is?

309
00:23:05,993 --> 00:23:09,195
The fact that you're there
when I get out of the water.

310
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,902
- Want to get in?
- Me?

311
00:23:14,895 --> 00:23:17,561
No, I'll just watch from here.

312
00:23:49,471 --> 00:23:50,914
Hey.

313
00:23:56,449 --> 00:23:58,021
Sung Sae Ryeong.

314
00:23:59,481 --> 00:24:01,889
Have you thought about that?

315
00:24:05,539 --> 00:24:07,006
Come on...

316
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:20,544
Your friend is terrifying.

317
00:24:20,544 --> 00:24:22,835
I might get punched if I cross her.

318
00:24:24,084 --> 00:24:27,340
I was so scared my heart was pounding.

319
00:24:28,264 --> 00:24:29,692
Could you tell?

320
00:24:55,634 --> 00:24:57,411
Hey, hey!

321
00:24:58,555 --> 00:25:00,416
Get out.

322
00:25:00,416 --> 00:25:05,374
I have seen it all before anyway.
It's nothing new.

323
00:25:05,374 --> 00:25:07,310
Wait, no...

324
00:25:07,310 --> 00:25:10,436
I'm not curious at all.

325
00:25:10,436 --> 00:25:12,694
Get out. Hurry up and get out.

326
00:25:12,694 --> 00:25:13,892
What...

327
00:25:28,403 --> 00:25:29,866
Have you eaten?

328
00:25:32,714 --> 00:25:35,388
I asked if you ate anything.

329
00:25:36,870 --> 00:25:40,310
Don't cling to me. Get off.

330
00:25:40,310 --> 00:25:42,125
Why?

331
00:25:42,125 --> 00:25:45,023
There's no reason for us
to be stuck together like this.

332
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,914
Then explain this.

333
00:25:57,410 --> 00:25:59,852
Who told you to dig through my drawer?

334
00:25:59,852 --> 00:26:02,230
It's not like I have never seen your face.

335
00:26:02,910 --> 00:26:04,749
First time seeing it at your place.

336
00:26:08,132 --> 00:26:10,059
It's just that I couldn't throw it away.

337
00:26:14,156 --> 00:26:17,110
So you couldn't throw it away.

338
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:20,998
You kept it so carefully
in a little box on the console by your bed...

339
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:29,661
I still like you, just like you still like me.

340
00:26:32,342 --> 00:26:34,387
Thank you for liking me.

341
00:26:34,387 --> 00:26:37,910
I'm grateful, but I'm just asking if you ate.

342
00:26:37,910 --> 00:26:42,476
I liked you from the first moment.
You did too, right?

343
00:26:42,476 --> 00:26:44,770
Yes, you always say that.

344
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:46,266
So did you eat? Food.

345
00:26:46,266 --> 00:26:49,660
I want to sleep with you.

346
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:56,034
Why do I understand all this...

347
00:26:56,034 --> 00:26:57,994
Why do I know it?

348
00:26:57,994 --> 00:27:00,479
Because it's what you say every time we meet.

349
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,094
Listen carefully.

350
00:27:04,094 --> 00:27:06,416
No, look carefully.

351
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:07,626
Me too.

352
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:09,627
I like you.

353
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:10,995
But...

354
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,566
We can't be together now.

355
00:27:14,508 --> 00:27:18,136
Why not? Why! Why!

356
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:22,516
Because I'm too busy to take care
of anyone or to do anything.

357
00:27:22,516 --> 00:27:23,600
I'm not free.

358
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:27,125
I haven't taken my specialist exam,
and I haven't done military service.

359
00:27:27,125 --> 00:27:28,689
So I can't go out with--

360
00:27:28,689 --> 00:27:30,978
I'm very independent.

361
00:27:30,978 --> 00:27:32,610
I know...

362
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:34,363
You don't want to sleep with me?

363
00:27:34,363 --> 00:27:35,914
No, that's not...

364
00:27:35,914 --> 00:27:38,448
No, that's not what I mean.

365
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:39,910
Hey--

366
00:27:39,910 --> 00:27:41,275
Hey...

367
00:27:42,703 --> 00:27:44,663
You said you like me.

368
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:46,102
I like you.

369
00:27:46,102 --> 00:27:49,325
I do like you, but, Dul Hee, right now I--

370
00:28:03,842 --> 00:28:08,366
Just the two of you are really
going to the Seoul house?

371
00:28:09,294 --> 00:28:10,399
Yes.

372
00:28:11,441 --> 00:28:13,263
You're not going anywhere else?

373
00:28:14,394 --> 00:28:16,111
No.

374
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,444
I'll call when we get there.

375
00:28:17,444 --> 00:28:18,963
I'll call.

376
00:28:20,673 --> 00:28:22,734
Then call as soon as you arrive.

377
00:28:22,734 --> 00:28:24,805
Right when we arrive is tough.

378
00:28:24,805 --> 00:28:25,956
Yes.

379
00:28:25,956 --> 00:28:27,502
I'll call tomorrow morning.

380
00:28:27,502 --> 00:28:29,198
And I have a lot of assignments.

381
00:28:30,461 --> 00:28:34,506
Fine. Let's say Jung Yeon does his
homework in Seoul.

382
00:28:34,506 --> 00:28:37,706
Kim Ha Yeon, what will you do in Seoul?

383
00:28:45,014 --> 00:28:46,476
Go for it.

384
00:28:47,706 --> 00:28:49,377
What?

385
00:28:49,377 --> 00:28:52,499
I want to cheer myself on, Mom.

386
00:28:53,593 --> 00:28:55,218
What is she talking about?

387
00:29:23,781 --> 00:29:25,448
Jung Yeon.

388
00:29:25,448 --> 00:29:26,525
Yes?

389
00:29:28,101 --> 00:29:30,263
About summer.

390
00:29:30,263 --> 00:29:31,432
Yes.

391
00:29:33,398 --> 00:29:35,826
It's not over already, is it?

392
00:29:49,781 --> 00:29:51,581
- Was it a tough day?
- No.

393
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:53,140
- Hello.
- Hello.

394
00:30:01,385 --> 00:30:03,748
You little rascal.

395
00:30:05,286 --> 00:30:08,316
Just how far do you intend to go?

396
00:30:09,604 --> 00:30:11,415
To the end of this competition.

397
00:30:11,415 --> 00:30:12,779
Is that so?

398
00:30:12,779 --> 00:30:16,135
And if my abilities allow, the next one too.

399
00:30:16,135 --> 00:30:18,414
Keep pushing until I leave here for good.

400
00:30:18,414 --> 00:30:20,198
Cho Yu Gyeom!

401
00:30:22,072 --> 00:30:27,744
Honey, Yu Gyeom has an important swim meet.

402
00:30:27,744 --> 00:30:30,944
It's the finals qualifier, so I...

403
00:30:32,234 --> 00:30:34,318
Send Yu Gyeom to Uiseong!

404
00:30:34,318 --> 00:30:38,248
Put a tutor on him in the guesthouse
and don't let him out for the whole break.

405
00:30:38,248 --> 00:30:42,345
- If he still isn't himself after the break!
- Father.

406
00:30:43,302 --> 00:30:44,778
Honey.

407
00:30:44,778 --> 00:30:46,303
Father.

408
00:30:46,303 --> 00:30:48,804
Please forgive my rudeness,
but I have to say this.

409
00:30:49,473 --> 00:30:50,861
I...

410
00:30:51,471 --> 00:30:56,415
have never wanted to be a member of
this family for even a single moment.

411
00:30:56,415 --> 00:30:58,382
What did you say?

412
00:30:58,382 --> 00:30:59,585
Not once.

413
00:30:59,585 --> 00:31:02,143
How could I?

414
00:31:02,143 --> 00:31:07,358
My husband is wrapped up in another woman,
and doesn't even know if I'm here or what I do.

415
00:31:07,358 --> 00:31:08,358
Honey.

416
00:31:08,358 --> 00:31:09,678
Father.

417
00:31:09,678 --> 00:31:13,558
Still, I thought of myself
as the lady of the house.

418
00:31:13,558 --> 00:31:17,647
But someone told me
that I'm not the lady of the house.

419
00:31:17,647 --> 00:31:20,598
That I'm just someone who works
in this house's kitchen.

420
00:31:20,598 --> 00:31:23,451
So I thought about it. It's true.

421
00:31:23,451 --> 00:31:28,229
I report to the kitchen in the morning
and clock out at nine at night.

422
00:31:28,889 --> 00:31:32,867
There is one difference between me
and the people who work in the kitchen.

423
00:31:33,685 --> 00:31:37,438
They go home once their work is over.

424
00:31:37,438 --> 00:31:42,249
And there, a family welcomes them warmly.

425
00:31:43,862 --> 00:31:45,805
But I don't, Father.

426
00:31:45,805 --> 00:31:47,824
Get up. First, get up and...

427
00:31:47,824 --> 00:31:50,911
Please don't say this man is my family.

428
00:31:50,911 --> 00:31:54,414
He has no interest in me.

429
00:31:54,414 --> 00:31:57,336
And he can't do anything on his own.

430
00:31:58,198 --> 00:31:59,781
Father.

431
00:31:59,781 --> 00:32:03,534
A head of the household should do something
for the family, right?

432
00:32:03,534 --> 00:32:06,718
But Jae Jin doesn't.

433
00:32:06,718 --> 00:32:10,480
And you made him that way.

434
00:32:11,578 --> 00:32:13,044
Father.

435
00:32:13,678 --> 00:32:19,678
You're turning my son into
the same kind of man as Jae Jin.

436
00:32:21,335 --> 00:32:23,813
I really can't stand that.

437
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:30,824
If you hate it that much, leave right now.

438
00:32:30,824 --> 00:32:32,605
I want to leave too.

439
00:32:32,605 --> 00:32:34,329
But in this house...

440
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,802
It's not just Jae Jin.

441
00:32:38,958 --> 00:32:41,962
My children are here too.

442
00:32:41,962 --> 00:32:46,965
Father, I promise you right here and now.

443
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:51,830
I will never bring this up again
for the rest of my life.

444
00:32:51,830 --> 00:32:55,614
I'll keep quietly working
in the kitchen as I do now.

445
00:32:56,758 --> 00:32:58,570
But Yu Gyeom...

446
00:32:59,188 --> 00:33:02,201
Just Yu Gyeom, please
don't let him live like his father.

447
00:33:02,201 --> 00:33:03,886
Father...

448
00:33:05,298 --> 00:33:08,878
Yu Gyeom entering the competition now
doesn't mean he'll win first place.

449
00:33:08,878 --> 00:33:12,824
But, Father, at least let him earn
his own chances.

450
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:17,118
Don't stop him from getting
the results that come with them.

451
00:33:17,118 --> 00:33:23,759
Things like that are truly more than
enough with my husband alone, Father.

452
00:33:23,759 --> 00:33:25,102
Please.

453
00:33:29,801 --> 00:33:31,133
Fine.

454
00:33:33,658 --> 00:33:34,878
Go.

455
00:33:37,476 --> 00:33:38,921
Go.

456
00:33:47,869 --> 00:33:49,865
Listen.

457
00:33:49,865 --> 00:33:53,605
I'll send him, but not
because I agree with you.

458
00:33:54,765 --> 00:33:57,340
It's because I don't want to lose you.

459
00:34:35,119 --> 00:34:37,995
So we're dating now, right?

460
00:34:46,910 --> 00:34:49,773
We are dating, right?

461
00:34:53,399 --> 00:34:55,228
I told you.

462
00:34:55,844 --> 00:34:57,478
How could we date?

463
00:34:57,478 --> 00:35:01,423
I'm too busy, and you're still too young.

464
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:10,108
After what we did together just a moment ago,
you're telling me I'm too young?

465
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:12,529
No, I don't mean it like that.
It's just that right now...

466
00:35:12,529 --> 00:35:18,529
You sleep with me and then dump me?

467
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:21,458
No, I can't dump you.

468
00:35:21,458 --> 00:35:23,758
No, I won't dump you.

469
00:35:23,758 --> 00:35:26,842
But you know, you're still immature.

470
00:35:26,842 --> 00:35:29,752
So aren't you immature too?

471
00:35:29,752 --> 00:35:31,616
No, of course I'm not.

472
00:35:31,616 --> 00:35:34,095
I don't live cut off from my parents
like you do.

473
00:35:34,843 --> 00:35:38,313
You know why I live like this!

474
00:35:40,710 --> 00:35:42,899
Do you really want to date me?

475
00:35:42,899 --> 00:35:44,380
Yes.

476
00:35:44,380 --> 00:35:47,858
Then go down there
and fix your family problems first.

477
00:35:47,858 --> 00:35:50,619
The estrangement with your family.
Fix that first.

478
00:35:52,704 --> 00:35:57,408
Why do I have to make up with my family
just because we're dating?

479
00:35:59,576 --> 00:36:01,603
Because I'm going to marry you.

480
00:36:05,499 --> 00:36:07,638
Dad! Why are you so late?

481
00:36:07,638 --> 00:36:09,292
Your grandfather caught me.

482
00:36:09,292 --> 00:36:11,127
Really? And then?

483
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:13,922
We got out. Get them there safely.
Drive carefully.

484
00:36:13,922 --> 00:36:14,964
- Okay, Dad.
- Okay.

485
00:36:14,964 --> 00:36:17,008
And call me when you arrive.

486
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,031
- Yes.
- Yes.

487
00:36:18,031 --> 00:36:20,347
By the way, Sam Hee.

488
00:36:20,347 --> 00:36:21,518
Yes, Dad.

489
00:36:21,518 --> 00:36:23,093
Who is that?

490
00:36:25,100 --> 00:36:26,478
My girlfriend.

491
00:36:26,478 --> 00:36:27,971
- Right.
- No, no.

492
00:36:27,971 --> 00:36:31,327
I mean, this man.

493
00:36:31,327 --> 00:36:34,317
Hello. I'm...

494
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:37,686
Hello. He's my brother. My real brother.

495
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:39,989
Yes.

496
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:44,510
We're off.

497
00:36:44,510 --> 00:36:46,373
- Okay, go.
- I'm going.

498
00:36:46,373 --> 00:36:48,123
Goodbye.

499
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:49,781
Bye!

500
00:36:57,426 --> 00:37:03,240
But Sam Hee, I think your dad looked
at my brother like he was a thief.

501
00:37:04,831 --> 00:37:08,812
Sam Hee, I saw you put a heart
next to this guy's name.

502
00:37:08,812 --> 00:37:13,311
My dad's a bit overprotective,
and I haven't really dated anyone before...

503
00:37:13,311 --> 00:37:14,693
What?

504
00:37:14,693 --> 00:37:16,299
What are you doing, Jung Yeon?

505
00:37:20,170 --> 00:37:22,950
Ha Yeon... it's Ha Yeon, right?

506
00:37:22,950 --> 00:37:23,970
Yes?

507
00:37:23,970 --> 00:37:26,786
Sorry, but your hand...

508
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:27,964
Let go.

509
00:37:37,663 --> 00:37:41,720
Then take off the heart you put
next to his name.

510
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:43,663
That kind of bugged me.

511
00:37:45,508 --> 00:37:47,695
You put a heart next to my name?

512
00:37:48,769 --> 00:37:49,889
Yes!

513
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:53,434
What?

514
00:38:16,213 --> 00:38:21,070
I find dating women hard.

515
00:38:21,070 --> 00:38:23,077
Dating someone I like is even harder.

516
00:38:23,077 --> 00:38:24,596
Because nobody understands me.

517
00:38:24,596 --> 00:38:28,196
But you said you understand me.

518
00:38:28,828 --> 00:38:31,010
Then I want to marry you.

519
00:38:31,010 --> 00:38:32,770
What about you?

520
00:38:32,770 --> 00:38:34,337
I have no one but you.

521
00:38:37,103 --> 00:38:39,302
Then go make up with your parents.

522
00:38:40,730 --> 00:38:44,530
Go down there and say
you won't live that way anymore.

523
00:38:44,530 --> 00:38:50,090
If you come back after begging them for
forgiveness, you can live here from then on.

524
00:38:54,142 --> 00:38:56,685
Or not, if you don't want to.

525
00:38:56,685 --> 00:38:58,336
If you don't want to, forget it.

526
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:04,543
I'm going down. I'm going. Seriously!

527
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:11,793
So you can say "seriously" in sign language.

528
00:39:12,990 --> 00:39:14,719
That's impressive, really.

529
00:39:16,563 --> 00:39:18,400
I'll go down and apologize! Happy?

530
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:22,519
[Men's 200m Freestyle
Final Qualifying Round Three]

531
00:39:29,083 --> 00:39:31,143
Glad you came, Cho Yu Gyeom.

532
00:39:32,790 --> 00:39:34,398
Not me.

533
00:39:36,619 --> 00:39:38,661
- Can I hit him?
- No.

534
00:39:38,661 --> 00:39:42,076
From what I hear, Jeong Uk has
suffered plenty at your hands too.

535
00:39:43,550 --> 00:39:48,557
Hey, anyway, you both need to do well today.

536
00:39:48,557 --> 00:39:53,370
I mean, you two always
did well, but look at this.

537
00:39:53,370 --> 00:39:56,148
Baek Seung Woo. He broke into the 47s.

538
00:39:57,950 --> 00:40:02,730
Hey, he beat your best record in just one race.

539
00:40:02,730 --> 00:40:07,160
Hey, isn't his worst time your best time?

540
00:40:07,160 --> 00:40:08,744
Such burning competitiveness.

541
00:40:08,744 --> 00:40:10,846
This is why I trust you two so much.

542
00:40:10,846 --> 00:40:12,619
Come on, hands in.

543
00:40:12,619 --> 00:40:15,050
Yes, hands in. Let's go. One, two, three!

544
00:40:15,050 --> 00:40:16,483
- Upo!
- Upo!

545
00:40:16,483 --> 00:40:18,458
- Fighting!
- Fighting!

546
00:40:18,458 --> 00:40:20,417
- Fighting!
- All right.

547
00:40:20,417 --> 00:40:22,891
We're starting. Athletes, gather round.

548
00:40:24,341 --> 00:40:26,748
- Fighting!
- Stay focused, Cho Yu Gyeom.

549
00:40:29,552 --> 00:40:30,688
What's wrong?

550
00:40:31,350 --> 00:40:33,071
You can't go in?

551
00:40:34,070 --> 00:40:35,462
I can't.

552
00:40:54,994 --> 00:41:00,961
Hello? A friend of Si Ha's is here.

553
00:41:00,961 --> 00:41:06,553
Because he has something to say.

554
00:41:19,230 --> 00:41:21,523
Please help me, Jung Yeon.

555
00:41:35,839 --> 00:41:37,322
Jung Yeon.

556
00:41:38,415 --> 00:41:40,513
Jung Yeon, we can come in...

557
00:41:55,390 --> 00:41:57,720
Come in... Please come in.

558
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:06,519
[Men's High School 200m Freestyle]

559
00:42:06,519 --> 00:42:08,590
Now, the Men's High School 200m Freestyle...

560
00:42:08,590 --> 00:42:12,494
Final qualifying round three.
Eight swimmers are entering.

561
00:42:12,494 --> 00:42:16,495
Many important swimmers are lined up today.

562
00:42:16,495 --> 00:42:18,453
There he is.

563
00:42:18,453 --> 00:42:21,341
But Sae Ryeong, why didn't you go there?

564
00:42:22,290 --> 00:42:24,869
Yu Gyeom's racing. Why didn't you go?

565
00:42:27,462 --> 00:42:29,670
- That's...
- Sung Sae Ryeong.

566
00:42:29,670 --> 00:42:33,470
- I need to talk to you.
- Now, the swimmers are at the starting blocks.

567
00:42:33,470 --> 00:42:37,829
The men's high school 200m freestyle
final qualifying round three.

568
00:43:20,312 --> 00:43:22,266
Eat.

569
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:23,286
Thank you.

570
00:43:25,910 --> 00:43:32,398
If anything, you were the one who
suffered because of our Si Ha.

571
00:43:56,968 --> 00:43:59,536
Thank you for coming.

572
00:43:59,536 --> 00:44:04,536
We had no one to give this to, so we kept it.

573
00:44:04,536 --> 00:44:06,676
What is this, Jung Yeon?

574
00:44:07,550 --> 00:44:09,733
This...

575
00:44:09,733 --> 00:44:13,364
We have no reason to accept this.

576
00:44:19,440 --> 00:44:21,199
This is...

577
00:44:22,287 --> 00:44:28,186
I borrowed some money from Si Ha.

578
00:44:29,002 --> 00:44:32,795
You may not know this, but...

579
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:37,580
What? But she wouldn't have had
that kind of money.

580
00:44:37,580 --> 00:44:39,006
No.

581
00:44:39,657 --> 00:44:41,247
She did.

582
00:44:44,538 --> 00:44:46,013
I...

583
00:44:47,771 --> 00:44:49,431
was going to pay it back.

584
00:44:51,150 --> 00:44:54,627
I promised I would.

585
00:44:57,074 --> 00:44:58,709
But I never got the chance.

586
00:45:00,038 --> 00:45:01,606
I never even repaid her.

587
00:45:03,607 --> 00:45:05,326
Si Ha...

588
00:45:08,089 --> 00:45:09,948
ended up like that...

589
00:45:16,160 --> 00:45:17,410
Young man.

590
00:45:17,410 --> 00:45:20,990
Thank you for not forgetting our Si Ha.

591
00:45:22,389 --> 00:45:24,989
Thank you.

592
00:45:28,077 --> 00:45:29,662
And thank you for keeping your promise.

593
00:45:41,322 --> 00:45:44,828
Early on, Im Jeong Uk is out in front
in first place.

594
00:45:44,828 --> 00:45:47,514
And shortly they'll make the 50m turn.

595
00:45:47,514 --> 00:45:50,434
Yes, Cho Yu Gyeom in lane four
is holding fourth place,

596
00:45:50,434 --> 00:45:52,160
Now, the 50m turn.

597
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:55,360
Last race, too, the hero of the final drama
was Cho Yu Gyeom.

598
00:45:55,360 --> 00:45:57,069
- That's right.
- Yes.

599
00:46:28,869 --> 00:46:31,494
- Over here, Yu Gyeom.
- Over here, Yu Gyeom.

600
00:46:31,494 --> 00:46:33,374
- Go on!
- A little more...

601
00:46:33,374 --> 00:46:38,020
- Im Jeong Uk's sprint is very strong as well.
- Yes.

602
00:46:38,020 --> 00:46:43,926
Now, Cho Yu Gyeom is closing the gap
on Im Jeong Uk.

603
00:46:43,926 --> 00:46:45,910
- Just like that.
- You never know.

604
00:46:45,910 --> 00:46:47,869
- Come on, go!
- Go get him!

605
00:46:47,869 --> 00:46:50,705
Just a little faster. Cho Yu Gyeom, hurry!

606
00:46:50,705 --> 00:46:53,212
At this rate, he...

607
00:46:53,940 --> 00:46:57,183
Now, nearing 150m.

608
00:47:00,360 --> 00:47:03,654
Now, Cho Yu Gyeom is sprinting on the way back.

609
00:47:03,654 --> 00:47:06,620
- Cho Yu Gyeom passes the swimmer in third.
- Yes.

610
00:47:06,620 --> 00:47:10,060
- Yes.
- Now only Im Jeong Uk is ahead of him.

611
00:47:10,060 --> 00:47:14,020
Cho Yu Gyeom's powerful sprint
is starting again.

612
00:47:14,020 --> 00:47:15,560
Cho Yu Gyeom, Cho Yu Gyeom.

613
00:47:15,560 --> 00:47:19,503
- Now, incredible!
- He passes him!

614
00:47:19,503 --> 00:47:22,619
- He passes!
- Cho Yu Gyeom, to the end,

615
00:47:22,619 --> 00:47:26,969
he'll keep speeding up. Cho Yu Gyeom
goes straight for the touch.

616
00:47:26,969 --> 00:47:29,256
Cho Yu Gyeom. Amazing!

617
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:37,993
Cho Yu Gyeom takes first!

618
00:47:37,993 --> 00:47:40,995
He takes first in 47.97!

619
00:47:40,995 --> 00:47:43,285
A rising star! A new star!

620
00:47:43,285 --> 00:47:44,910
Second place is Im Jeong Uk.

621
00:47:44,910 --> 00:47:49,660
First place goes to Cho Yu Gyeom
with a time of 47.97.

622
00:47:49,660 --> 00:47:51,205
Jeong Uk.

623
00:47:52,369 --> 00:47:54,666
- Good job.
- Look at the times.

624
00:47:54,666 --> 00:47:57,295
- Yes.
- Im Jeong Uk also posted an incredible time.

625
00:47:58,828 --> 00:48:00,174
They had a truly great race.

626
00:48:00,174 --> 00:48:04,507
Yes. And they're only eighteen.
Eighteen years old.

627
00:48:04,507 --> 00:48:06,929
- Yes.
- Must be his girlfriend.

628
00:48:06,929 --> 00:48:12,202
- She's so pretty.
- What? Isn't that Kim Ha Yeon?

629
00:48:12,202 --> 00:48:15,369
This race is getting interesting. What is that?

630
00:48:15,369 --> 00:48:21,369
That's right. The men's 200m freestyle final
qualifying round three was won by Cho Yu Gyeom.

631
00:48:24,110 --> 00:48:26,280
- I lent him.
- What?

632
00:48:26,280 --> 00:48:29,996
I lent Cho Yu Gyeom to her, that's all.

633
00:48:31,285 --> 00:48:33,918
What's there to talk about?
Let's take it outside.

634
00:48:36,241 --> 00:48:37,472
Aren't you coming?

635
00:48:47,680 --> 00:48:50,261
Sir, I heard your son took first place!

636
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:52,520
It's not even the finals.

637
00:48:52,520 --> 00:48:56,875
- They say he's a rising star! A star!
- Please. Hardly a star.

638
00:48:58,978 --> 00:49:00,437
Yes. I mean...

639
00:49:00,437 --> 00:49:02,025
[Changnyeong Myeongin]

640
00:49:02,025 --> 00:49:05,136
- Is it the one?
- Yes.

641
00:49:05,136 --> 00:49:08,722
This one has been losing
power for about a week now.

642
00:49:09,867 --> 00:49:11,669
We had one like this before
and fixed it, right?

643
00:49:11,669 --> 00:49:13,130
That one...

644
00:49:13,130 --> 00:49:15,100
There were a few like that.

645
00:49:15,100 --> 00:49:18,955
It's probably overheating because it's so hot.

646
00:49:22,090 --> 00:49:23,556
Then...

647
00:49:23,556 --> 00:49:25,869
Should we stop it? It could catch fire.

648
00:49:25,869 --> 00:49:29,439
But there's an order that
has to ship by tomorrow.

649
00:49:31,930 --> 00:49:33,720
Then...

650
00:49:33,720 --> 00:49:38,309
Then should we run it just until today
and call a mechanic tomorrow?

651
00:49:38,309 --> 00:49:42,376
Let me go ask my father first.

652
00:49:42,376 --> 00:49:45,035
I would like to stop it, though.

653
00:49:45,035 --> 00:49:48,327
Then please ask the elder and let me know.

654
00:49:48,327 --> 00:49:49,574
Okay.

655
00:50:08,964 --> 00:50:09,970
What?

656
00:50:09,970 --> 00:50:11,296
Ready to kill me?

657
00:50:11,296 --> 00:50:12,366
Yes.

658
00:50:12,366 --> 00:50:14,338
I'm going to kill you today.

659
00:50:14,338 --> 00:50:17,723
- Forget Yu Gyeom. I'm going to--
- I'm sorry.

660
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:18,767
What?

661
00:50:21,276 --> 00:50:23,816
I said I'm sorry.

662
00:50:23,816 --> 00:50:27,081
For everything I did to you all this time.

663
00:50:27,081 --> 00:50:29,255
Yes. I'm sorry for all of it.

664
00:50:30,155 --> 00:50:32,225
What did you do to me?

665
00:50:34,700 --> 00:50:37,750
I didn't treat you like a person. I used you.

666
00:50:37,750 --> 00:50:41,619
I didn't even think of you as a friend.
I pushed you around.

667
00:50:41,619 --> 00:50:44,971
I always treated you carelessly.

668
00:50:44,971 --> 00:50:47,471
I dumped my emotional garbage on you.

669
00:50:47,471 --> 00:50:50,300
I ignored you in front of people. I lied.

670
00:50:51,636 --> 00:50:52,776
All right.

671
00:50:52,776 --> 00:50:58,809
You could kill me right now,
that's how cruel I was to you.

672
00:50:58,809 --> 00:51:01,007
I'm sorry for that, Kim Jin Mi.

673
00:51:03,456 --> 00:51:05,861
Why are you suddenly saying this?

674
00:51:07,971 --> 00:51:12,364
When I was being bullied,
Kim Ha Yeon said this.

675
00:51:12,364 --> 00:51:14,175
Are you miserable?

676
00:51:18,596 --> 00:51:22,169
The kids you bullied probably
felt the same way.

677
00:51:23,122 --> 00:51:25,249
She also told me something.

678
00:51:25,249 --> 00:51:29,325
The kids I bullied would want
a sincere apology from me.

679
00:51:30,577 --> 00:51:34,454
Honestly, I didn't understand that at all.

680
00:51:35,846 --> 00:51:37,379
But now...

681
00:51:38,341 --> 00:51:40,046
I understand.

682
00:51:42,451 --> 00:51:45,936
When you all were bullying me, I thought...

683
00:51:45,936 --> 00:51:47,464
Later...

684
00:51:48,314 --> 00:51:53,682
Later, if you just
apologize to me, I'll be fine.

685
00:51:58,827 --> 00:52:00,791
I'm truly sorry.

686
00:52:01,873 --> 00:52:03,842
I'm sorry, Kim Jin Mi.

687
00:52:04,798 --> 00:52:07,687
I was wrong. I'm really sorry.

688
00:52:38,729 --> 00:52:40,244
What?

689
00:52:40,244 --> 00:52:43,256
You're so pretty. I want to keep you to myself.

690
00:52:43,256 --> 00:52:44,397
What?

691
00:52:45,582 --> 00:52:47,741
Well...

692
00:52:49,014 --> 00:52:54,531
I really don't understand.
What's with that girl?

693
00:52:57,262 --> 00:52:58,905
- Sir.
- What?

694
00:52:59,888 --> 00:53:02,186
This is according to my information.

695
00:53:03,124 --> 00:53:05,787
The word is that she's the real deal.

696
00:53:06,456 --> 00:53:08,376
Then what's Sung Sae Ryeong?

697
00:53:08,376 --> 00:53:10,976
Sir! That's why I'm so confused!

698
00:53:10,976 --> 00:53:12,619
Get it?

699
00:53:12,619 --> 00:53:16,322
Hey, don't run. You little brat, stay still.

700
00:53:17,611 --> 00:53:18,786
Father.

701
00:53:18,786 --> 00:53:22,661
Wouldn't it be better to just stop it?
A fire would be much worse.

702
00:53:22,661 --> 00:53:23,996
I'll take a look.

703
00:53:23,996 --> 00:53:26,582
But it's had problems for several days now,
Father.

704
00:53:26,582 --> 00:53:28,134
Still...

705
00:53:31,115 --> 00:53:32,679
Jae Jin.

706
00:53:32,679 --> 00:53:33,736
Yes?

707
00:53:33,736 --> 00:53:36,036
Were you happy?

708
00:53:36,036 --> 00:53:37,214
Pardon? Father?

709
00:53:37,214 --> 00:53:41,322
I mean, were you happy when you swam?

710
00:53:43,619 --> 00:53:45,556
Let's go.

711
00:53:45,556 --> 00:53:46,828
Jeez.

712
00:53:51,937 --> 00:53:52,983
Where is he?

713
00:53:52,983 --> 00:53:59,130
The boss had trouble with a machine,
so he went to the family home to get the elder.

714
00:53:59,130 --> 00:54:02,227
He never decides anything on his own.

715
00:54:03,202 --> 00:54:06,926
So is Yu Gyeom coming here today?

716
00:54:07,676 --> 00:54:10,463
Yu Gyeom will probably...

717
00:54:11,874 --> 00:54:14,046
Oh my, Father!

718
00:54:14,670 --> 00:54:18,043
I have something important to tell you, Father.

719
00:54:18,043 --> 00:54:20,500
- Let's go.
- Wait. Father!

720
00:54:23,436 --> 00:54:25,097
Why are you here again?

721
00:54:26,816 --> 00:54:28,496
Why did you come back?

722
00:54:28,496 --> 00:54:31,869
Because I can't go to that house!
So I came here instead!

723
00:54:31,869 --> 00:54:34,104
You ask why I came? Why?

724
00:54:34,104 --> 00:54:35,734
Yu Gyeom doesn't even come here.

725
00:54:35,734 --> 00:54:39,776
Then tell him to come here. You can ask him!

726
00:54:39,776 --> 00:54:41,320
Cho Jae Jin!

727
00:54:41,320 --> 00:54:46,010
If you keep me from seeing Yu Gyeom like this,
do you know what I'll tell him?

728
00:54:46,010 --> 00:54:47,727
Sam Hee.

729
00:54:47,727 --> 00:54:48,744
Where's Yu Gyeom?

730
00:54:48,744 --> 00:54:53,165
He came by train, so he's probably
on the city bus by now.

731
00:54:53,165 --> 00:54:57,805
Call Yu Gyeom's side and tell him
to come straight to Changnyeong Myeongin.

732
00:54:58,636 --> 00:55:00,763
The machine's a bit hot.

733
00:55:00,763 --> 00:55:02,973
It'll be fine, right?

734
00:55:04,698 --> 00:55:09,431
So, as for that order, how
much more do we have to make?

735
00:55:09,431 --> 00:55:10,812
We're about halfway.

736
00:55:10,812 --> 00:55:12,892
We'll run it all night to finish.

737
00:55:12,892 --> 00:55:14,712
Is that so?

738
00:55:14,712 --> 00:55:17,620
Then I'll look after it. You all go home.

739
00:55:17,620 --> 00:55:21,952
And at the office, leave only the few
people who are needed.

740
00:55:21,952 --> 00:55:23,244
We can stay longer...

741
00:55:23,244 --> 00:55:26,448
No. You worked hard, so go home. Go on.

742
00:55:26,448 --> 00:55:30,329
What else does an old man have to do?
I'll keep an eye on this.

743
00:55:32,352 --> 00:55:34,207
You all worked hard.

744
00:55:40,560 --> 00:55:42,226
Let's see.

745
00:55:59,952 --> 00:56:02,405
It's running fine. Good.

746
00:56:17,657 --> 00:56:18,910
Father.

747
00:56:19,963 --> 00:56:22,066
You called me here for this?

748
00:56:27,471 --> 00:56:29,356
My son. What's gotten into you lately?

749
00:56:29,356 --> 00:56:31,014
Is it teenage angst?

750
00:56:31,014 --> 00:56:33,752
- Mom will...
- You're my aunt!

751
00:56:33,752 --> 00:56:37,076
Why am I your son? An aunt is an aunt!

752
00:56:38,612 --> 00:56:40,480
Yu Gyeom.

753
00:56:40,480 --> 00:56:43,135
What did Mom do wrong?

754
00:56:43,135 --> 00:56:46,556
Mom just missed you so much.

755
00:56:58,132 --> 00:57:01,611
Send me a photo as proof when you get there.

756
00:57:02,502 --> 00:57:04,923
If you get caught lying, you know what happens.

757
00:57:08,136 --> 00:57:10,389
Summer's really over now.

758
00:57:10,389 --> 00:57:13,323
They're getting ready for the autumn harvest.

759
00:57:39,247 --> 00:57:41,069
- What?
- There's a fire. The fire over there!

760
00:57:42,629 --> 00:57:44,961
119! 119!

761
00:57:44,961 --> 00:57:48,400
[Changnyeong Myeongin]

762
00:58:03,972 --> 00:58:05,510
Dul Hee, Dul Hee.

763
00:58:05,510 --> 00:58:06,570
Did you report it?

764
00:58:06,570 --> 00:58:08,744
I did. They'll be here soon.

765
00:58:08,744 --> 00:58:14,704
Then go ring the alarm.
There might be people inside.

766
00:58:25,464 --> 00:58:27,350
You scared me!

767
00:58:28,072 --> 00:58:29,810
What? Why are you here, Dul Hee?

768
00:58:29,810 --> 00:58:32,892
You get out. You can't be here.

769
00:58:32,892 --> 00:58:35,933
I mean, why are you here?

770
00:58:37,124 --> 00:58:39,141
Fire.

771
00:58:39,141 --> 00:58:40,452
Fire?

772
00:58:40,452 --> 00:58:42,234
What are you talking about?

773
00:58:45,776 --> 00:58:49,392
Grab that and follow me. Quick.

774
00:58:55,327 --> 00:58:57,412
There's a fire? Where?

775
00:58:57,412 --> 00:58:59,206
- Reported it. Alarm's on.
- A fire?

776
00:58:59,206 --> 00:59:01,959
Everyone's out, but no fire trucks yet.

777
00:59:01,959 --> 00:59:03,919
Well, it looks perfectly fine to me.

778
00:59:03,919 --> 00:59:07,543
Sam Hee! A fire? What are you talking about?

779
00:59:07,543 --> 00:59:11,172
Mom. Dul Hee saw it from her taxi.
She says there's a fire here.

780
00:59:11,172 --> 00:59:13,192
Is everyone out?

781
00:59:13,192 --> 00:59:15,546
- Is no one inside?
- No, I hit the alarm.

782
00:59:15,546 --> 00:59:17,558
Really? That's a relief.

783
00:59:17,558 --> 00:59:18,987
Father.

784
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:21,391
Father is still inside!

785
00:59:21,391 --> 00:59:24,007
- Sir, the elder is...
- The elder is...

786
00:59:41,456 --> 00:59:42,792
Drop that and run.

787
00:59:59,474 --> 01:00:03,934
- I didn't see it. I just heard...
- I'm going in. Sir, just a moment.

788
01:00:03,934 --> 01:00:06,077
Father. Wait, please!

789
01:00:06,077 --> 01:00:10,527
I'm the owner here! Wait,
just a moment! Father.

790
01:00:10,527 --> 01:00:12,632
Where's Dul Hee? Isn't Dul Hee here?

791
01:00:12,632 --> 01:00:14,823
Yu Gyeom! Where's Yu Gyeom?

792
01:00:14,823 --> 01:00:16,551
Father.

793
01:02:11,327 --> 01:02:12,804
- Dul Hee! Dul Hee!
- Dul Hee!

794
01:02:12,804 --> 01:02:14,891
Dul Hee, Dul Hee!

795
01:02:47,222 --> 01:02:49,228
Yu Gyeom.

796
01:02:49,228 --> 01:02:54,194
They say there are three things
a person can never hide.

797
01:02:54,842 --> 01:03:00,720
A cough, poverty,
